learnings:
  - The build hole was only half the broken-serve story — fixing the stale-dist build wiring exposed a SECOND latent bug (canvas's `/files/*` Express-4 wildcard crashed serve on boot under Express 5). A live smoke test (boot serve, curl health) caught it; a build-passing check alone would not have. Always boot the actual server, not just build it.
  - 'Subtractive-then-additive paid off immediately: the surface the audit marked for deletion (canvas) was the exact thing blocking the launcher. Cutting dead chrome unblocked the spearhead rather than competing with it.'
  - Canvas was the audit's clearest 'delete not defer' call and it held up — stub serializer, zero .canvas files, no substrate linkage, AND actively harmful (boot crash). Defer-to-someday would have left serve broken.
